    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/02/puma-foreverrun-nitro-2-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Dual-density Nitro foam (softer core, firmer outer frame) gives a highly cushioned, moderately soft ride with good impact protection; heel transitions are smooth and the forefoot feels comfortable with a mild rocker and moderate flexibility.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is clearly bouncy and can support uptempo pace changes, but the foam is not especially snappy at top speed and works best at steady easy-to-moderate efforts.",
        "Stability: Mild-to-moderate guidance comes from tall sidewalls, a wider base, firmer medial/lateral foam, and heel-midfoot external reinforcements; the heel counter is moderately stiff and lateral support is strong without a traditional post.",
        "Durability: Outsole wear is minimal after about 75 miles, grip remains strong, and the midsole has retained resiliency and bounce, indicating above-average material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/02/puma-forever-run-nitro-2-multi-tester.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The co-molded dual-density NITRO midsole (softer core, firmer carrier) provides plush, recovery-oriented impact protection, with a deeper forefoot cushion feel than v1 and heel-friendly rocker/10 mm drop.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is described as deliberate and measured rather than highly bouncy or snappy; it handles mild pace pickups but is not a speed-focused ride.",
        "Stability: Stability is a major strength from the broad platform, wider midfoot vs v1, Run Guide geometry, and secure rear hold, but the heel counter/TPU clip can feel over-rigid laterally and may overcorrect for some runners.",
        "Durability: Reviewers characterize the shoe as durable/long-lasting, praise PumaGrip outsole performance, and expect strong foam longevity, though explicit long-term outsole wear data is limited in the text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/puma-foreverrun-nitro-2-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The added 2 mm stack (38 mm heel / 28 mm forefoot) fixed the prior forefoot cushion issue and gives a plush, protective ride with balanced softness.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is moderately bouncy and springy, with a quick, smooth heel-to-toe transition from the 10 mm drop/rocker setup rather than a sharp, snappy pop.",
        "Stability: RunGuide dual-density design (firmer rim + softer core) and heel clip provide strong, natural guidance; PWRTape and upper structure improve midfoot/lateral hold and reduce slippage.",
        "Durability: PumaGrip outsole is described as best-in-class with strong wet-weather grip and no notable wear concerns mentioned during testing, indicating solid outsole/material longevity."
      ]
    }
  ],
